OpenSSL 4.1.0: the ECH client resumes a session in the outer handshake after a rejection

Kuicksilver's own code, the sixth patch carried under ADR-0019 (docs/adr/0019-openssl-4-and-ech.md), applied after
openssl-4.1.0-ech-ee-checks.patch; pinned by its SHA-256 in gradle/openssl.toml as patch_6, applied by
tools/openssl/apply-patch.pl to the verified tarball, and dropped with the first OpenSSL release that fixes it (upstream
report drafted 2026-11-19, to be filed). Applies to OpenSSL master at 4a5704abc6d2 on top of the patches before it (git apply; extensions_clnt.c is 99
lines further down there).

The bug: RFC 9849 section 6.1.2: "If ECH is rejected and the client-facing server replies with a "pre_shared_key"
extension in its ServerHello, then the client MUST abort the handshake with an "illegal_parameter" alert."
tls_parse_stoc_psk (extensions_clnt.c) accepts identity 0 although the outer ClientHello carried only a GREASE PSK, and
goes on with the inner session's key.

The fix: when ECH was offered (not GREASE) and not accepted, a pre_shared_key in the ServerHello is illegal_parameter.

diff --git a/ssl/statem/extensions_clnt.c b/ssl/statem/extensions_clnt.c
--- a/ssl/statem/extensions_clnt.c
+++ b/ssl/statem/extensions_clnt.c
@@ -2451,8 +2451,22 @@
 
     if (!PACKET_get_net_2(pkt, &identity) || PACKET_remaining(pkt) != 0) {
         SSLfatal(s, SSL_AD_DECODE_ERROR, SSL_R_LENGTH_MISMATCH);
+        return 0;
+    }
+
+#ifndef OPENSSL_NO_ECH
+    /*
+     * ECH offered and rejected: our ClientHelloOuter only had a GREASE PSK,
+     * and the server may not resume in the outer handshake (RFC 9849,
+     * section 6.1.2)
+     */
+    if (s->ext.ech.es != NULL && s->ext.ech.attempted == 1
+        && s->ext.ech.success != 1
+        && s->ext.ech.grease != OSSL_ECH_IS_GREASE) {
+        SSLfatal(s, SSL_AD_ILLEGAL_PARAMETER, SSL_R_BAD_PSK_IDENTITY);
         return 0;
     }
+#endif
 
     if (identity >= (unsigned int)s->ext.tick_identity) {
         SSLfatal(s, SSL_AD_ILLEGAL_PARAMETER, SSL_R_BAD_PSK_IDENTITY);
